WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.520
- [Announcer] This satellite
image shows a convoy

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.200
of more than 20 vehicles linked

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.850
to the Wagner mercenary group entering

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.550
the cell military base in Belarus.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.930
Here on July 17,

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.753
hundreds of tents and
facilities fill the camp.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:17.460
32 days earlier, none of this was here.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.590
The growth of the base
signals that the private army

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:23.070
is relocating large numbers
of personnel and equipment.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.050
That's following the
deal brokered by Belarus

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.530
that curtailed the group's
June 24 drive towards Moscow

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.800
to demand the removal of
Russia's military leadership.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.170
So here's how the campers expanded

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.690
and the likely route the
vehicles linked to Wagner took

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.540
following the group's aborted mutiny.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.500
A video posted by a pro-Russia
war correspondent in mid-July

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.350
shows a convoy of trucks
and cars heading north

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.540
on the M-4 highway in Russia.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.000
Another clip shared by the
same account shows vehicles

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.780
driving approximately 73
miles north on the same road.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.640
Some of them can be seen with Wagner flags

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.993
hanging out of the windows.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.510
Across the border in Belarus,

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:03.780
this video captures yet another
convoy of similar vehicles

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.573
a 15-minute drive away from the cell camp.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.350
Military analysts say satellite
imagery shows vehicles

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.960
of the same make and
color exiting the highway

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.240
and entering the base.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.910
The vehicles seen in these
videos and images likely traveled

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.823
through Russia into
Belarus along this route.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.430
That's based on data from Janes,

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.560
a group which has been
tracking Wagner's movements

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.120
using social media video

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.850
and additional clips
geo located by Storyful.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.640
Janes said it tracked
at least 260 vehicles

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.600
in separate convoys between
the 11th and 18th of July.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.700
Images from the following
week showed dozens

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.730
of pickup trucks, minivans,
cars and heavy lift trailers

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.023
parked at the facility.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.410
Analysts say their characteristics
match what was seen

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.970
in the social media videos,

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.860
and the timing of their arrival indicates

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.783
they were from Wagner-linked convoys.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.650
The movements are the
largest public showing linked

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.590
to the mercenary group since
the failed march on Moscow.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.290
Military analysts say it
could indicate preparations

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.293
for the arrival of a large group
of equipment and personnel.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.010
The previously vacant facility

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.830
is also being adjusted
to be more habitable.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.480
Smoke or steam is being emitted

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.630
from a stack in these images,
analysts from Janes say,

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.040
suggesting it's being used

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.993
for electrical generation or heating.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.510
In addition, a vehicle position

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.760
next to the communication
tower in this image

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.280
indicates that he's being ready for use.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.320
Analysts say there are
limited other reasons

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.543
why a vehicle would
need to be parked there.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.420
Living facilities have also been built

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.010
potentially indicating plans

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.293
for a more permanent presence at the base.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:42.150
Analysts at Janes and Maxar
said latrines have been placed

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.060
along the outer perimeter of
the tent deployment areas,

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.403
and rows of outdoor
sinks are also present.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.120
The expansion of the camp
comes amid speculation

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.100
over Wagner's next moves.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.710
The whereabouts of the group's
leader, Yevgeny Prigozhin,

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.590
have been in question
since the failed mutiny.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:00.000
This social media footage

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.370
which has been geo
located to the cell base

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:06.163
purportedly shows the Wagner
leader welcoming troops.

00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:09.643
(Yevgeny speaking in foreign language)

00:03:09.643 --> 00:03:13.860
(troops speaking in foreign language)

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.050
While military analysts
say it's still unclear what

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:19.410
the expansion of the cell camp
ultimately means for Wagner,

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:23.089
this location may play a key
role in the group's future.

00:03:23.089 --> 00:03:25.756
(pensive music)

